{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123998","id":4683636629,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABFyqflQ","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123998","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123998.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123998.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123998","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123998/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123998/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123998/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/c6b553f308fb8b8d2ac371f238fa7e2ceca8594d","number":123998,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Fix inconsistent hashing of CallableCustomMethodPointers","user":{"login":"stenja","id":8284125,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgyODQxMjU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8284125?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stenja","html_url":"https://github.com/stenja","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stenja/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stenja/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stenja/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stenja/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stenja/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stenja/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stenja/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stenja/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stenja/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes #119740\r\n- Closes #119752\r\n- Closes #89657\r\n- Closes #95512\r\n- Closes #87626\r\n- Reverts #120394\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\nThe root cause of these issues is a bug in the hashing of CallableCustomMethodPointers, which meant some HashMap lookups in the connection/disconnection of signals were failing when they should have succeeded. \r\n\r\n#120394 attempted to band-aid over this bug by moving `new` operators out of the memory.h header so they wouldn't be inlined. This probably worked for some configurations, but I was still seeing the bug with gcc 16.2.1 20260810 and lto=full.\r\n\r\nThe actual bug is `CallableCustomMethodPointerBase::_setup`. The callers of `_setup` would all call it with `_setup((uint32_t *)&data, sizeof(Data));`. That mostly works, but casting `Data*` to `uint32_t*` violates strict aliasing and was technically undefined behavior. Newer versions of gcc with -flto were aggressive enough to take advantage of that UB and were hashing stale/garbage values. It's not actually a GCC bug like #120394 speculated. Since it's technically UB GCC is allowed to do this in its optimization pass.\r\n\r\nThe fix is changing the signature of `_setup` to take a `std::byte*` instead of `uint32_t*`. Casting a `Data*` to a `std::byte*` (or `char*`, but `std::byte` is more descriptive of what we're doing here) is allowed following strict aliasing. `_setup` then has to put those bytes into a real `uint32_t`, and we've correctly signaled to the compiler what it is we're actually doing: taking the byte representation of `data`, treating it as uint32_t, and hashing.\r\n\r\nI think the reason #120394 nudging the compiler to not inline `new` helped is that the main culprit of the bug was that the calls to `_setup` were in constructors, so the compiler wasn't able to catch this \"optimization\" of hashing garbage instead of `data` when `new` wasn't inlined.  The `std::byte` fix addresses the root cause of the issue, and fixes the issue even when `new` is inlined, so I went ahead and reverted that change. There's no reason we shouldn't be inlining new now that the root cause of the bug is fixed, and as far as I can tell, this bug was the only reason for that change.  If we do want to avoid inlining `new` for some other reason, I'm happy to undo that reversion.","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ak